--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.tsx is a dedicated page wrapper that promotes the Tesla "Feature Flags"
surface to a first-class route: `PageContainer(title=t('featureConfig.title'), subtitle=
t('featureConfig.subtitle'))` hosting the shared `<FeatureToggles/>` component
(web/src/features/settings/components/FeatureToggles.tsx). FeatureToggles renders the GlassPanel
header (Flag IconBox + title + subtitle + "Synced …" + Refresh button) and the feature table /
EmptyState with its full data-state set. The page's OWN parity surface is exactly the two
PageContainer strings; the embedded component is a SEPARATE, already-shipped P3 parity unit. On the
web the title/subtitle appear in the page chrome AND again in the component header — the native page
reproduces that faithfully (it is not a bug to "dedupe").

The native FeatureToggles component already exists at full parity (P3) in this repo:
  apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/FeatureToggles{,.Model,.Adapter,.Views,.Previews,.Tests}.swift
  — a `FeatureTogglesModel(source:telemetry:toast:)` that renders loading / content / empty / error /
  stale / offline. This P7 page is the WRAPPER that hosts it at /tesla-features (it does NOT
  re-implement it).

