OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`. That path does
NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real, compiled canonical
admin-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where every sibling P7 admin page ships
(ApiPlayground / DiskForecast / FleetTelemetryCoverage / LiveSignalInspector / SchemaDrift / AuditLog /
ApiLogs / APIKeys / FleetAPI / GDPRExport / RbacMatrix / FeatureFlags / TeslaOrders) and which
project.yml already lists via `- path: Sources`. The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Admin`.
This is the identical reconciliation the peer admin P7 logs recorded; no project.yml change is needed.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the dedicated top-level path `/tesla-features` (like `/api-playground`
→ `.apiPlayground`). A new `AppRoute.teslaFeatures` case is added (pathSegment "tesla-features";
systemImage "flag.fill" — matching the web `Flag` icon + the existing Layout.Nav catalog entry; group
`.account` — matching the web sidebar "Account" section where /tesla-features lives). `AppRouteParser`
auto-resolves "/tesla-features" → .teslaFeatures via pathSegment. `TeslaFeatureFlagsRouteRegistration`
hosts the page on .teslaFeatures and is chained into the TeslaSyncApp `\.routeHosts` registry.
RouteTests asserts the deep link. Recorded here per covenant #9.

